    {
      "id": "temperature",
      "status": "source-backed",
      "interpretation": "Temperature payload, directed channel, endpoint ports and typed exchange. Local interface/end/item names are representational choices; endpoint direction and payload come from the input.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "S1",
          "startLine": 4,
          "endLine": 4,
          "quote": "TemperatureReading, CoolingCommand, and EnableCommand are distinct exchanged item types. Probe's readings port is an output Temperature channel and controller's readings port is its input conjugate. Controller's cooling port outputs a Cooling channel to actuator's conjugated cooling port. Operator's enable port outputs an Enable channel to Cooler's conjugated enable boundary port; controller also has a conjugated enable port. Define the channel port types with the respective directed item, and explicit typed interfaces with flows for the two internal exchanges and the operator exchange; bind the boundary enable port to controller.enable. Do not treat connector direction as item-flow direction."
        }
